From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:49:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a per-turn restart carries foreground commands,
 keeps the hub's socket and relays the API across pods

With gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn a carried turn's foreground command is no longer moved to the
background at SIGTERM: it finishes on the old gateway with its real result. Background processes go to the next
gateway once no carried turn is in a tool round, and the device plugin's sockets stay open until then. The hub's
Webapp socket keeps its session past the seal, so carried turns stream on with no gap, and ends once the next
gateway is ready and the socket is idle, its client sent a request, or a carried turn moved over. A relayed device
leg closes with 1001 instead of 1012, and a relayed session socket only when idle. The standby opens its API port
before it takes over and publishes it in gateway.standby; the old pod relays API connections there and holds an API
request made between the restart and the release instead of answering 503. A prompt listed again under the same
id is announced once.
